 "The advantage of this practice is that when the market is high, the same money buys fewer units, and when the market is low, it buys more, so over time the cost is automatically averaged, and the psychological pressure of timing is avoided, with no need to agonize daily over whether to enter now.",
 "It suits office workers with stable income and no time to watch the market daily; as long as they persist, time often stands on the side of the patient, and smooth costs plus long-term compounding let small sums gradually accumulate into a tower.",
 "When buying funds, there are also a few small points worth knowing.",
 "The price of a fund is called its net asset value, calculated once after the market closes each day, representing how much each unit is currently worth.",
 "Both buying and redeeming incur certain fees according to the rules, and for frequent traders, fees accumulating day by day amount to a considerable sum, so the more frequent the short-term in-and-out, the more returns are eroded by fees.",
 "When choosing a fund, rather than looking only at who rose most sharply in the past year, it is better to examine how it fared through several rounds of ups and downs, whether long-term performance is stable, whether the fund manager is stable, and whether the assets it holds match one's own temperament.",
 "Some people, seeking convenience, simply split their money into several parts and invest in several funds of different styles, letting them complement each other, so that when the east is dark the west is bright.",
 "This idea of diversified allocation is the same as not putting all eggs in one basket.",
 "Beginners should also be reminded to avoid several common traps.",
 "The first is staring only at short-term rankings, buying whichever rose most recently, yet rankings change every year, and by the time one chases in, it often happens to be right at the peak.",
