 "The third is taking money meant for long-term investment and making frequent short-term in-and-out trades, ending up with little return but plenty of fees paid.",
 "Those who truly benefit on this road are mostly people who set goals, choose their products, and then persist quietly; they are not led by emotion through temporary rises and falls but keep their eyes on three to five years ahead.",
 "Fund investing, in the final analysis, is a patient long race; it is not about who charges hardest but about who can steadily complete the whole course.",
 "At the entry stage, a few plain principles must also be kept in mind.",
 "First, invest within your means, using only spare money you will not need for three to five years, and never put in money meant for meals, medical care, or children's education, or you may be forced to sell at a low point in an emergency.",
