 "Third, know your own risk tolerance; those with impatient temperaments who cannot bear paper losses should not force themselves into highly volatile products, and an investment that keeps you up at night does not suit you.",
 "Funds are not a myth of guaranteed profit without loss; they too rise and fall and can be painful in bear markets, but compared with stock trading on one's own, they leave the professional matters to professionals and reduce risk through diversification; for most ordinary families they are a gentler and sustainable path to wealth accumulation that, given time, often yields reassuring results.",
 "For families just starting out, it is advisable to begin with a small monthly fixed investment, first getting familiar with the fluctuations of net asset value, then gradually increasing the proportion invested.",
